{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CHECKPOINT — peak-window pause (operator-ordered 5-11am PT). NOT STARTED beyond planning.\n\nSTATE: plan written into the description and PASSED review-plan; ticket claimed/in_progress. ZERO code or docs edits made — nothing is staged, committed, or pushed for this ticket. The worktree ../operator-batch2 (branch operator-batch2) is clean at commit e57ca52587, which belongs to rasbora, not to this ticket.\n\nRESUME PLAN, unchanged from the description: add the standing rule to AGENTS.md as one bullet plus a narrowed clause on the existing 'The gate' bullet (which today reads 'comment recheck if it is a flake'); reconcile CONTRIBUTING.md section 6's 'Verified -1 but the failure looks transient/flaky' bullet so it splits environmental faults from test nondeterminism; add tests/unit/test_flaky_test_guidance.py pinning both the new rule and the ABSENCE of the old retry-until-green licence.\n\nTwo facts confirmed during planning, worth not re-deriving: the /rebar-debug skill lives at examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md, and no existing test pins the 'recheck if it is a flake' wording in either AGENTS.md or CONTRIBUTING.md, so narrowing them breaks nothing. docs/dependency-advisory-runbook.md already states the same shape for its own gate and is consistent, so it needs no edit.\n\nIronic and worth noting on resume: this session's own CI selection hit the hammerkop order-dependent decline-test flake, which is precisely the class this ticket's rule says to debug rather than retry."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786622295595975001,"uuid":"527ea19f-03ca-4f21-adf8-8f0922856dec"}